WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.052
A query asks whether A causes B.

00:00:03.227 --> 00:00:05.849
Two candidate passages contain exactly the

00:00:05.869 --> 00:00:10.075
same words: A causes B, and B causes A.

00:00:10.238 --> 00:00:12.241
Would counting matching terms distinguish

00:00:12.261 --> 00:00:15.295
them? Pause and identify what information

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.648
determines relevance.

00:00:19.048 --> 00:00:21.818
The word inventory is identical; direction

00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:24.847
differs. A missing relationship is not

00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:27.746
automatically a missing vocabulary entry.

00:00:27.895 --> 00:00:30.568
Negation, causal direction and the binding

00:00:30.588 --> 00:00:33.494
of two concepts can fail even when lexical

00:00:33.514 --> 00:00:35.684
overlap is complete and the query is

00:00:35.704 --> 00:00:36.547
familiar.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.943
Another failure appears across settings.

00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:42.509
A retriever works plausibly on ordinary

00:00:42.529 --> 00:00:45.073
web questions but poorly on biomedical

00:00:45.093 --> 00:00:47.985
papers or high recall evidence searches.

00:00:48.134 --> 00:00:50.897
Investigate out of distribution transfer:

00:00:51.098 --> 00:00:53.114
deployment may differ from the retrieval

00:00:53.134 --> 00:00:55.575
conditions represented during training.

00:00:56.137 --> 00:00:59.170
The chapter identifies three useful sites:

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.521
query shift in style or intent; corpus or

00:01:02.541 --> 00:01:05.432
domain shift in discipline, genre,

00:01:05.711 --> 00:01:08.784
language or time; and task or relevance

00:01:08.804 --> 00:01:10.420
shift in the relationship that should

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.255
rank. Every word can be familiar while the

00:01:13.275 --> 00:01:15.884
rewarded retrieval behaviour is wrong for

00:01:15.904 --> 00:01:16.786
the task.

00:01:17.696 --> 00:01:20.192
Training pairs, negatives and relevance

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:21.855
judgements teach what should rank

00:01:21.875 --> 00:01:24.986
together. Finding one answer bearing web

00:01:25.006 --> 00:01:27.473
passage rewards something different from

00:01:27.493 --> 00:01:29.651
recovering all studies meeting review

00:01:29.671 --> 00:01:32.448
criteria, finding a known item or

00:01:32.468 --> 00:01:34.174
discovering citations.

00:01:34.349 --> 00:01:36.378
More synonyms do not repair that

00:01:36.398 --> 00:01:38.040
difference by themselves.

00:01:38.592 --> 00:01:41.315
Conversely, one new discipline can combine

00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:44.446
distribution shift, specialised vocabulary

00:01:44.466 --> 00:01:46.288
and mismatched terminology.

00:01:46.464 --> 00:01:48.685
These hypotheses can overlap.

00:01:48.861 --> 00:01:50.902
Out of distribution is a training to

00:01:50.922 --> 00:01:53.969
deployment relationship, not a synonym for

00:01:53.989 --> 00:01:56.109
a strange word or an unexplained bad

00:01:56.129 --> 00:01:56.791
result.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.850
The hypothesis becomes stronger when

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.298
plausible performance on familiar queries

00:02:02.318 --> 00:02:04.643
degrades systematically for a discipline,

00:02:04.792 --> 00:02:07.916
collection, query style or purpose.

00:02:08.065 --> 00:02:10.172
Compare locally using known relevance

00:02:10.192 --> 00:02:13.574
evidence before adapting, retraining or

00:02:13.594 --> 00:02:14.823
replacing a model.

00:02:14.998 --> 00:02:17.246
Undisclosed training data limits what can

00:02:17.266 --> 00:02:18.199
be concluded.

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:20.789
The chapter cites BEIR’s heterogeneous

00:02:20.809 --> 00:02:24.332
zero shot evaluation: BM twenty five was a

00:02:24.352 --> 00:02:27.232
robust baseline, while some more expensive

00:02:27.252 --> 00:02:29.693
neural and reranking approaches performed

00:02:29.713 --> 00:02:30.865
better on average.

00:02:31.028 --> 00:02:33.495
That benchmark finding is not a universal

00:02:33.515 --> 00:02:36.897
law about lexical or dense transfer, nor a

00:02:36.917 --> 00:02:38.739
new comparison run here.

00:02:39.624 --> 00:02:41.459
Now return to the relation problem.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.908
Boolean logic preserves the explicit

00:02:43.928 --> 00:02:46.872
inclusion and exclusion you state over

00:02:46.892 --> 00:02:48.211
analysed terms.

00:02:48.374 --> 00:02:51.524
Ordinary conjunction still does not encode

00:02:51.544 --> 00:02:52.876
who caused what.

00:02:53.026 --> 00:02:55.416
Simply excluding a word is different from

00:02:55.436 --> 00:02:57.619
correctly interpreting the scope of a

00:02:57.639 --> 00:02:59.036
negated proposition.

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:02.347
Phrase operators, positional indexes and

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:05.556
proximity can preserve adjacency and local

00:03:05.576 --> 00:03:08.455
order. They are useful controls to test,

00:03:08.643 --> 00:03:10.981
but adjacency alone does not solve

00:03:11.001 --> 00:03:14.176
causality, negation or relation binding.

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:16.226
Our opposite statements are controlled

00:03:16.246 --> 00:03:19.203
text contrasts, not predictions of any

00:03:19.223 --> 00:03:21.083
particular system’s scores.

00:03:21.981 --> 00:03:25.267
A cross encoder reads query and candidate

00:03:25.287 --> 00:03:27.419
together, offering the strongest

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:29.906
architectural opportunity to model these

00:03:29.926 --> 00:03:32.908
relationships. Late interaction preserves

00:03:32.928 --> 00:03:35.575
more token evidence than a pooled vector,

00:03:35.738 --> 00:03:38.243
but still encodes the query and document

00:03:38.263 --> 00:03:40.228
separately. Neither architecture

00:03:40.248 --> 00:03:42.560
guarantees correct logic.

00:03:43.131 --> 00:03:45.962
The cited NevIR evaluation found cross

00:03:45.982 --> 00:03:48.719
encoders strongest and late interaction

00:03:48.739 --> 00:03:52.057
next, yet most evaluated systems still

00:03:52.077 --> 00:03:54.827
ranked at or below a random baseline.

00:03:55.002 --> 00:03:56.464
Keep that qualification.

00:03:56.639 --> 00:03:59.673
And no reranker can rescue a paper absent

00:03:59.693 --> 00:04:02.005
from its first stage shortlist.

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:04.916
The chapter contrasts three reference

00:04:04.936 --> 00:04:07.442
patterns. Strict Boolean preserves

00:04:07.462 --> 00:04:10.431
explicit logic over analysed terms.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:14.168
BM twenty five preserves lexical evidence,

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:17.003
especially rare matching terms.

00:04:17.178 --> 00:04:19.633
Single vector dense retrieval preserves

00:04:19.653 --> 00:04:21.797
overall learnt similarity.

00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:23.924
Each has characteristic strengths and

00:04:23.944 --> 00:04:25.238
blind spots.

00:04:25.796 --> 00:04:28.248
This is not an exhaustive list: learnt

00:04:28.268 --> 00:04:30.606
sparse and late interaction methods can

00:04:30.626 --> 00:04:33.389
also retrieve first stage candidates.

00:04:33.564 --> 00:04:36.224
Transformation changes inputs, control

00:04:36.244 --> 00:04:39.072
selects operations, and rerankers compare

00:04:39.092 --> 00:04:41.650
shortlists. A product saying it uses

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:44.498
vectors does not tell you which evidence

00:04:44.518 --> 00:04:46.443
its full pipeline preserves.

00:04:47.354 --> 00:04:49.842
Begin with a known relevant record or

00:04:49.862 --> 00:04:52.574
controlled contrast and establish that it

00:04:52.594 --> 00:04:53.862
could have been returned.

00:04:54.024 --> 00:04:56.414
Then inspect terminology, component

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.850
vocabularies, training transfer and

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.814
relationships. Save the available evidence

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.527
and mark unknowns.

00:05:03.689 --> 00:05:05.975
Several failures can coexist.

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:09.245
Test a remedy against the suspected cause:

00:05:09.472 --> 00:05:12.906
expansion, an exact lexical route, local

00:05:12.926 --> 00:05:16.797
adaptation, explicit logic, reranking or a

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:17.918
combined system.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:20.844
No representation preserves everything

00:05:20.864 --> 00:05:23.473
equally well. Diagnosis supplies

00:05:23.493 --> 00:05:26.424
hypotheses. Chapter fourteen asks how to

00:05:26.444 --> 00:05:28.898
compare them and decide what better

00:05:28.918 --> 00:05:30.650
retrieval means for the task.
